    <sys:String x:Key="str.Tip.LiveWalker.GWorldDepth">Maximum pointer hops to search downward from GWorld when using "Locate in GWorld" (default 7). Larger = finds deeper targets but slower.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="str.Toolbar.GWorldDepth">Locate in GWorld depth</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="str.Toolbar.GWorldDeep">Deep (nested containers)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="str.Tip.LiveWalker.GWorldDeep">Deep "Locate in GWorld" (default off — the analogue of Value Search's Deep). When on, the path search ALSO follows object pointers stored inside one struct-array / struct-set / struct-map element level (e.g. an actor referenced only from Inventory[3].ItemActor), so otherwise-unreachable objects can be located; and a bare value address inside a deeply-nested container is attributed to its owner instead of failing. Heavier — it reads each struct-array's elements per visited node.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="str.Toolbar.DeepScanElemCap">Deep container scan cap</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="str.Tip.Toolbar.DeepScanElemCap">Per-container element probe cap for the Instances "Lookup" deep scan — the recursive descent that finds a value buried in nested containers (e.g. SaveSlotList[1]…Tunes[N]). Only runs when the fast shallow lookup finds nothing. Higher = reaches values at higher element indices but slower; default 256.</sys:String>
